1
00:02:56,682 --> 00:02:57,773
Captain!

2
00:03:38,974 --> 00:03:40,735
Is that a trench?

3
00:03:42,478 --> 00:03:44,269
It looks like there's more of them inside.

4
00:03:49,234 --> 00:03:51,285
Echo 2-6 to command.

5
00:03:52,029 --> 00:03:54,368
Colonel, we've got eyes
on three Kong in the north woods.

6
00:03:54,448 --> 00:03:57,121
One of them is armed. And our donkey
just spotted another trench.

7
00:03:57,201 --> 00:03:58,622
Maybe the base is near.

8
00:03:59,953 --> 00:04:01,004
Yes, sir.

9
00:04:03,665 --> 00:04:05,626
Yes, sir, copy. Over.

10
00:04:10,798 --> 00:04:12,339
Hey, donkey.

11
00:04:18,263 --> 00:04:19,104
Preacher.

12
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,521
The one with the gun.

13
00:04:26,688 --> 00:04:29,236
As soon as the gunner's down,
you guys take out the trench.

14
00:04:29,316 --> 00:04:30,317
Yes, sir.
Yes, sir.

15
00:04:50,462 --> 00:04:51,303
Fire!

16
00:04:58,887 --> 00:05:00,218
Come on!

17
00:06:21,428 --> 00:06:22,639
Reload!

18
00:07:18,819 --> 00:07:20,820
Fall back! Fall back!

19
00:07:43,552 --> 00:07:45,513
Colonel, do you copy? Colonel!

20
00:07:45,888 --> 00:07:46,809
Who is this?

21
00:07:46,889 --> 00:07:48,310
Preacher, sir! It's Preacher!

22
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:50,437
Where are you, soldier? I need your position.

23
00:07:50,517 --> 00:07:52,815
I don't know!
What do you see?

24
00:07:52,895 --> 00:07:54,400
I can't see anything, sir.

25
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,610
We lost a lot of men,
and the captain is dead, sir.

26
00:07:56,690 --> 00:07:58,821
Okay, calm down. You're in command now.

27
00:07:59,401 --> 00:08:00,781
Command, sir?

28
00:08:00,861 --> 00:08:02,616
I think it's just me all by myself now.

29
00:08:02,696 --> 00:08:04,027
Take control.

30
00:08:07,201 --> 00:08:09,581
Colonel, I don't think
I'm gonna make it, sir.

31
00:08:09,661 --> 00:08:10,833
I'm sorry.

32
00:08:10,913 --> 00:08:12,126
I'm so sorry, sir.

33
00:08:12,206 --> 00:08:15,167
Listen to me. You kill as many as you can.

34
00:08:19,922 --> 00:08:22,093
No! No, no!

35
00:09:37,624 --> 00:09:39,545
Sixty-three dead.

36
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:45,921
You're him.

37
00:09:46,925 --> 00:09:48,126
You're Caesar.

38
00:09:49,803 --> 00:09:51,814
We've been searching for you for so long.

39
00:09:52,639 --> 00:09:56,438
We heard you had a hidden command base.
But we could never find it.

40
00:09:56,518 --> 00:09:58,899
Some of us started to think
that you might be dead.

41
00:09:58,979 --> 00:10:00,901
But Colonel McCullough said
you were out here somewhere.

42
00:10:00,981 --> 00:10:02,778
Just kill us already.
Shut up, man!

43
00:10:02,858 --> 00:10:04,780
What? They're animals.

44
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:06,781
He's gonna slaughter us.

45
00:10:13,744 --> 00:10:17,835
I did not start this war.

46
00:10:19,458 --> 00:10:22,539
The ape who did is dead.

47
00:10:24,004 --> 00:10:26,345
His name was Koba.

48
00:10:27,049 --> 00:10:28,630
I killed him.

49
00:10:30,552 --> 00:10:33,809
Now, I fight only...

50
00:10:33,889 --> 00:10:35,561
to protect apes.

51
00:10:35,641 --> 00:10:36,732
Yeah?

52
00:10:39,061 --> 00:10:40,062
What about him?

53
00:10:41,021 --> 00:10:43,022
We've got 10 more just like him.

54
00:10:44,024 --> 00:10:45,985
I know these apes.

55
00:10:46,902 --> 00:10:49,153
They follow Koba.

56
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:52,371
They tried to kill me.

57
00:10:53,033 --> 00:10:56,290
They fear what I will do to them.

58
00:10:56,370 --> 00:11:00,001
So now, they serve you.

59
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:02,254
Just to survive.

60
00:11:04,753 --> 00:11:07,554
I don't fear you.

61
00:11:11,427 --> 00:11:14,428
You must fear.

62
00:11:15,222 --> 00:11:19,355
How long you think woods can protect you?

63
00:11:19,435 --> 00:11:22,276
Humans destroy you.

64
00:11:23,439 --> 00:11:27,440
Their Kerna has all power.

65
00:11:28,235 --> 00:11:32,196
For them, he more than just human.

66
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,455
He everything.

67
00:11:36,535 --> 00:11:40,506
He say: First Caesar die...

68
00:11:41,790 --> 00:11:45,251
then all of you die.

69
00:11:52,342 --> 00:11:54,553
Winter! Take this traitor outside!

70
00:12:02,019 --> 00:12:04,850
What should we do with the humans?

71
00:12:18,577 --> 00:12:19,948
You're letting us go?

72
00:12:20,746 --> 00:12:24,037
Tell your Colonel you have seen me now...

73
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:27,381
and I have a message for him.

74
00:12:27,461 --> 00:12:31,672
Leave us the woods, and the killing can stop.

75
00:12:41,767 --> 00:12:45,107
Do you think they will give him the message?

76
00:12:45,187 --> 00:12:47,188
They are the message, Maurice.

77
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,031
He will see we are not savages.

78
00:12:59,034 --> 00:13:02,375
The traitor attacked me! He got away!

79
00:13:29,606 --> 00:13:30,897
Koba...

80
00:13:31,692 --> 00:13:33,243
still haunts us.

81
00:13:35,529 --> 00:13:37,785
Why didn't I see...

82
00:13:37,865 --> 00:13:42,166
that he could not forgive
what humans did to him?

83
00:13:44,705 --> 00:13:47,836
No one could have known how much darkness...

84
00:13:47,916 --> 00:13:50,957
...was living inside him.

85
00:14:25,370 --> 00:14:27,661
Father...

86
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:44,935
Welcome home, Rocket.

87
00:14:45,015 --> 00:14:47,266
You look tired.

88
00:14:48,268 --> 00:14:49,479
It was a long journey.

89
00:14:49,853 --> 00:14:52,234
Father, we found something!

90
00:14:52,523 --> 00:14:53,654
Come.

91
00:15:20,592 --> 00:15:21,843
Mother...

92
00:15:30,394 --> 00:15:31,695
Cornelius...

93
00:15:32,438 --> 00:15:34,149
Say hi to your brother!

94
00:15:43,198 --> 00:15:45,239
Look who's here, son...

95
00:15:56,128 --> 00:15:58,459
Lake...

96
00:16:27,701 --> 00:16:29,702
This is it, father...

97
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:32,211
We can start over... A new home.

98
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:36,001
What is beyond those mountains, son?

99
00:16:36,376 --> 00:16:38,127
Show them, Rocket...

100
00:16:50,891 --> 00:16:52,102
A desert!

101
00:16:52,518 --> 00:16:54,769
The journey is long...

102
00:16:55,270 --> 00:16:57,611
But that is why humans will not find us.

103
00:16:58,148 --> 00:17:00,779
We must leave tonight!

104
00:17:01,193 --> 00:17:03,615
Tonight? That's impossible!

105
00:17:03,695 --> 00:17:05,159
How long can we wait, Lake?

106
00:17:05,239 --> 00:17:07,120
Soldiers getting closer!

107
00:17:07,408 --> 00:17:08,159
Winter...

108
00:17:16,917 --> 00:17:19,708
Your son's been gone, Caesar...

109
00:17:20,671 --> 00:17:24,132
He doesn't know how hard it's been.

110
00:17:27,094 --> 00:17:29,555
I know you are scared...

111
00:17:30,431 --> 00:17:32,352
We all are...

112
00:17:32,891 --> 00:17:35,852
But we are still planning...

113
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,611
Yes.

114
00:17:40,566 --> 00:17:43,987
We must find a safe way out of the woods.

115
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:47,284
There were only two of you.

116
00:17:47,364 --> 00:17:50,585
But we are... many.

117
00:18:01,462 --> 00:18:04,973
We will find a way out of here.

118
00:18:07,509 --> 00:18:10,180
Apes together...

119
00:18:11,597 --> 00:18:13,098
strong.

120
00:19:22,501 --> 00:19:23,630
Stay here, son!

121
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:26,001
Protect your mother and brother!

122
00:20:10,549 --> 00:20:11,840
Caesar! What's wrong?

123
00:20:12,634 --> 00:20:13,725
How many on patrol?

124
00:20:14,595 --> 00:20:15,556
Five? Six?

125
00:20:15,804 --> 00:20:16,976
Get them!

126
00:20:17,056 --> 00:20:19,637
Luca, get Rocket, too.

127
00:21:12,319 --> 00:21:14,320
Lima four to command. Colonel, did you...

128
00:21:24,665 --> 00:21:25,794
Rocket!

129
00:21:25,874 --> 00:21:27,421
What happened?

130
00:21:27,501 --> 00:21:29,922
I heard him talking! The Colonel is here!

131
00:21:31,630 --> 00:21:34,051
99, target acquired.

132
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:39,475
99, target acquired. Repeat.
King Kong is dead.

133
00:21:39,555 --> 00:21:42,526
Let's go. I can get out from here.

134
00:23:48,934 --> 00:23:50,445
Caesar...

135
00:23:50,728 --> 00:23:52,479
We can't find Winter!

136
00:23:55,274 --> 00:23:59,075
He was scared! I think he betrayed us!

137
00:24:03,407 --> 00:24:06,408
Have you found Cornelius yet?

138
00:24:07,828 --> 00:24:10,079
We're still searching.

139
00:24:14,710 --> 00:24:17,711
Let's go look for Caesar's little son.

140
00:24:52,039 --> 00:24:53,040
Cornelius!

141
00:25:01,924 --> 00:25:03,595
You're safe now.

142
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:23,031
Lake...

143
00:25:24,071 --> 00:25:25,492
You loved my son.

144
00:25:26,407 --> 00:25:30,238
Look after his brother until I return.

145
00:25:35,332 --> 00:25:38,881
You're not coming with us to our new home?

146
00:25:38,961 --> 00:25:40,092
No.

147
00:25:44,675 --> 00:25:46,186
Go with Lake.

148
00:26:02,609 --> 00:26:03,900
Caesar!

149
00:26:04,236 --> 00:26:06,147
You're not going after them?

150
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:10,287
Not them. Him.

151
00:26:10,367 --> 00:26:14,368
Caesar, you are our leader!

152
00:26:14,955 --> 00:26:16,916
We can't leave without you!

153
00:26:17,499 --> 00:26:18,830
You must.

154
00:26:20,169 --> 00:26:22,424
The soldiers will be back soon.

155
00:26:22,504 --> 00:26:24,715
Father!

156
00:26:26,008 --> 00:26:27,596
When I find him...

157
00:26:27,676 --> 00:26:29,547
the soldiers will all come after me.

158
00:26:31,013 --> 00:26:34,224
That may give you the best chance
to get out of the woods.

159
00:26:37,853 --> 00:26:39,734
Where is he going?

160
00:26:43,650 --> 00:26:46,531
Caesar! Caesar!

161
00:27:35,702 --> 00:27:38,463
The soldiers' camp is always moving.

162
00:27:38,705 --> 00:27:40,826
My guards think they know where it is.

163
00:27:41,083 --> 00:27:42,334
Let me take you.

164
00:27:42,668 --> 00:27:44,999
You need me to back you up!

165
00:27:45,629 --> 00:27:46,960
No.

166
00:27:48,549 --> 00:27:49,720
Please...

167
00:27:50,426 --> 00:27:53,257
I know what it's like...

168
00:27:53,679 --> 00:27:55,260
...to lose a son.

169
00:27:56,306 --> 00:28:00,057
I may not make it back.

170
00:28:01,228 --> 00:28:04,519
That's why I'm coming.

171
00:28:06,275 --> 00:28:09,116
To make sure you do.

172
00:28:45,814 --> 00:28:48,025
Guards think soldiers here...

173
00:28:48,358 --> 00:28:50,689
Always fires burning.

174
00:29:04,083 --> 00:29:05,634
No one here...

175
00:29:06,335 --> 00:29:08,046
Search the area.

176
00:29:31,568 --> 00:29:33,649
I'm just gonna put this down.

177
00:30:08,147 --> 00:30:10,018
What's he doing out here alone?

178
00:30:10,524 --> 00:30:12,325
Maybe he's a deserter?

179
00:31:25,265 --> 00:31:26,676
Look around.

180
00:31:30,145 --> 00:31:31,766
Take what you can.

181
00:33:26,053 --> 00:33:27,641
Something wrong with her.

182
00:33:27,721 --> 00:33:29,182
I don't think she can speak.

183
00:33:31,725 --> 00:33:32,926
Come.

184
00:33:51,745 --> 00:33:55,826
She'll die out here alone.

185
00:33:56,583 --> 00:33:58,384
We cannot take her, Maurice.

186
00:34:03,257 --> 00:34:05,128
I understand...

187
00:34:05,718 --> 00:34:08,799
But I cannot leave her.

188
00:35:17,790 --> 00:35:20,921
Did you find the Colonel?

189
00:35:21,668 --> 00:35:22,709
No.

190
00:35:24,171 --> 00:35:25,552
Winter.

191
00:35:40,062 --> 00:35:41,403
Where's the Colonel?

192
00:35:50,906 --> 00:35:52,027
He's gone.

193
00:35:52,408 --> 00:35:53,409
Gone?

194
00:35:55,494 --> 00:35:56,875
He left this morning...

195
00:35:57,955 --> 00:36:00,086
...took many men with him.

196
00:36:00,833 --> 00:36:03,544
More soldiers are coming down from the North.

197
00:36:04,420 --> 00:36:06,421
The Colonel is going to meet them...

198
00:36:07,089 --> 00:36:08,670
...at the border.

199
00:36:09,717 --> 00:36:11,968
What border? Why?

200
00:36:16,724 --> 00:36:18,735
I don't know.

201
00:36:19,226 --> 00:36:21,767
But the rest of us are going tomorrow.

202
00:36:23,856 --> 00:36:27,187
The donkeys think the soldiers
from the North...

203
00:36:27,651 --> 00:36:31,112
...are coming to help finish off
the apes for good.

204
00:36:32,156 --> 00:36:35,027
That day, after the battle on the hill...

205
00:36:35,534 --> 00:36:39,045
The donkey we caught promised me
the Colonel would spare my life...

206
00:36:39,288 --> 00:36:42,709
If I told them where you were hiding.

207
00:36:44,168 --> 00:36:46,879
Forgive me!

208
00:36:51,133 --> 00:36:53,844
My son...

209
00:36:55,512 --> 00:36:59,143
my wife...

210
00:37:00,684 --> 00:37:02,145
are dead.

211
00:38:14,717 --> 00:38:17,138
Now what do we do?

212
00:38:17,511 --> 00:38:19,142
Wait till the soldiers go...

213
00:38:20,222 --> 00:38:23,103
Follow them to the Colonel.

214
00:38:56,425 --> 00:38:58,136
Koba!

215
00:38:58,719 --> 00:39:00,100
Ape...

216
00:39:01,263 --> 00:39:05,104
not kill ape.

217
00:39:14,276 --> 00:39:16,947
The soldiers are leaving!

218
00:39:54,650 --> 00:39:56,321
They stopped.

219
00:39:56,819 --> 00:39:57,820
Get down!

220
00:40:10,457 --> 00:40:12,748
What are they shooting at?

221
00:40:14,878 --> 00:40:16,839
I don't know.

222
00:41:39,588 --> 00:41:41,589
Why did they shoot you?

223
00:42:01,693 --> 00:42:03,364
Like her!

224
00:42:04,571 --> 00:42:06,572
He cannot speak!

225
00:42:10,244 --> 00:42:13,465
He will die of those wounds.

226
00:42:23,590 --> 00:42:25,181
Luca...

227
00:42:46,071 --> 00:42:47,910
Where did the soldiers go?

228
00:42:47,990 --> 00:42:51,951
Winter said they were going to a border.

229
00:42:52,202 --> 00:42:54,253
Yes, but which way is that?

230
00:46:42,599 --> 00:46:45,600
Bad Ape!

231
00:46:51,233 --> 00:46:53,944
Bad Ape.

232
00:46:56,739 --> 00:46:58,070
Who are you?

233
00:46:58,699 --> 00:47:01,030
What are you doing here?

234
00:47:03,704 --> 00:47:05,545
I don't think he understands.

235
00:47:08,459 --> 00:47:10,090
I don't recognize him.

236
00:47:10,544 --> 00:47:12,385
He's not one of us.

237
00:47:14,423 --> 00:47:15,764
Are you alone here?

238
00:47:36,028 --> 00:47:37,149
Cold?

239
00:47:53,921 --> 00:47:54,962
Cold.

240
00:48:00,636 --> 00:48:03,726
I see girl, I think you human.

241
00:48:03,806 --> 00:48:05,137
But you ape.

242
00:48:05,891 --> 00:48:07,312
Like me.

243
00:48:09,144 --> 00:48:10,655
No, put down.

244
00:48:11,480 --> 00:48:12,901
How long have you been here?

245
00:48:12,981 --> 00:48:14,320
Long time.

246
00:48:14,400 --> 00:48:16,861
Long, long time.

247
00:48:27,538 --> 00:48:28,619
Home.

248
00:48:30,165 --> 00:48:31,456
Old home.

249
00:48:37,214 --> 00:48:39,015
Are there more like you?

250
00:48:39,842 --> 00:48:41,764
More apes from zoo.

251
00:48:41,844 --> 00:48:44,435
Dead. All dead.

252
00:48:45,055 --> 00:48:46,096
Long time.

253
00:48:46,849 --> 00:48:49,350
Human get sick.

254
00:48:49,685 --> 00:48:52,356
Ape get smart.

255
00:48:53,021 --> 00:48:54,612
Then human kill ape.

256
00:48:55,107 --> 00:48:56,568
But not me.

257
00:48:56,942 --> 00:48:58,533
I run.

258
00:48:59,194 --> 00:49:01,205
You learn to speak...

259
00:49:01,530 --> 00:49:03,701
Listen. Human...

260
00:49:07,494 --> 00:49:09,045
"Bad Ape!"

261
00:49:11,248 --> 00:49:12,579
Bad Ape.

262
00:49:13,667 --> 00:49:14,998
No.

263
00:49:15,502 --> 00:49:17,003
No touch.

264
00:49:18,547 --> 00:49:20,378
That's mine.

265
00:49:26,638 --> 00:49:27,759
I'm okay!

266
00:49:37,900 --> 00:49:39,611
Amazing...

267
00:49:39,902 --> 00:49:42,073
Always thought we were the only ones.

268
00:49:42,404 --> 00:49:44,615
Wonder if there are more in the world?

269
00:49:45,157 --> 00:49:48,698
More apes like us.

270
00:49:51,205 --> 00:49:53,426
Eat! Eat.

271
00:49:56,418 --> 00:49:57,919
New friends.

272
00:49:58,378 --> 00:49:59,919
Special day.

273
00:50:04,426 --> 00:50:05,677
Where did you get this?

274
00:50:08,764 --> 00:50:09,935
Bad place.

275
00:50:11,266 --> 00:50:12,730
I find long time ago.

276
00:50:12,810 --> 00:50:15,441
After zoo, I look for food...

277
00:50:15,521 --> 00:50:18,112
I find human zoo.

278
00:50:18,690 --> 00:50:20,321
Zoo for sick.

279
00:50:21,443 --> 00:50:22,948
Big walls.

280
00:50:23,028 --> 00:50:25,949
Sick human climb.

281
00:50:27,116 --> 00:50:29,777
Bad human kill.

282
00:50:30,160 --> 00:50:33,417
And then, all get sick.

283
00:50:33,497 --> 00:50:35,668
All dead now for a long time.

284
00:50:36,417 --> 00:50:37,504
Long time.

285
00:50:37,584 --> 00:50:39,005
Bad humans?

286
00:50:40,921 --> 00:50:42,302
Soldiers?

287
00:50:45,050 --> 00:50:46,341
Soldiers.

288
00:50:46,802 --> 00:50:48,473
A deserted military camp!

289
00:50:48,846 --> 00:50:51,257
On the border!

290
00:50:51,849 --> 00:50:56,140
Maybe the Colonel
and the troops are going there?

291
00:50:56,979 --> 00:50:59,068
Is it far? Can you take us?

292
00:50:59,148 --> 00:51:00,986
Human zoo?

293
00:51:01,066 --> 00:51:03,817
No. No, no go back there.

294
00:51:04,903 --> 00:51:07,242
Everyone dead. I come here. Very safe here.

295
00:51:07,322 --> 00:51:08,577
Never go back.

296
00:51:08,657 --> 00:51:10,204
Please, you must take us!

297
00:51:10,284 --> 00:51:12,790
No! No! Cannot take!

298
00:51:12,870 --> 00:51:14,961
Cannot take. No! No!

299
00:51:17,040 --> 00:51:18,379
Look! Look!

300
00:51:18,459 --> 00:51:21,215
More snow. Cannot go. Must stay.

301
00:51:21,295 --> 00:51:23,342
You eat, you rest.

302
00:51:23,422 --> 00:51:25,513
Stay here with me.

303
00:51:27,551 --> 00:51:29,432
Here, you keep.

304
00:51:32,681 --> 00:51:34,182
She keep.

305
00:52:02,002 --> 00:52:03,343
Who is...

306
00:52:09,426 --> 00:52:10,717
child?

307
00:52:11,887 --> 00:52:13,558
I don't know.

308
00:52:14,723 --> 00:52:18,064
But she with you.

309
00:52:20,604 --> 00:52:22,405
She has no one else.

310
00:52:29,154 --> 00:52:32,575
I see you look at her just now.

311
00:52:35,786 --> 00:52:38,367
Look sad.

312
00:52:42,918 --> 00:52:45,089
You have child?

313
00:52:48,257 --> 00:52:49,258
One.

314
00:52:52,094 --> 00:52:54,605
The other was killed by human.

315
00:52:57,182 --> 00:52:58,603
Soldier?

316
00:53:15,576 --> 00:53:18,447
I had child.

317
00:53:24,752 --> 00:53:27,753
You think you will find him...

318
00:53:30,966 --> 00:53:32,467
at human zoo?

319
00:53:37,890 --> 00:53:39,181
With soldier?

320
00:53:42,853 --> 00:53:44,854
I don't know.

321
00:53:46,982 --> 00:53:48,483
Maybe.

322
00:53:50,819 --> 00:53:51,900
Then...

323
00:53:57,159 --> 00:54:00,450
maybe I take you.

324
00:55:43,432 --> 00:55:44,773
Thirsty.

325
00:55:46,769 --> 00:55:48,520
Thirsty.

326
00:55:51,648 --> 00:55:52,609
Thirsty.

327
00:56:07,748 --> 00:56:10,629
Luca, come. Let's go closer.

328
00:56:10,709 --> 00:56:12,040
Keep them safe.

329
00:56:18,342 --> 00:56:20,222
What are they doing?

330
00:56:20,302 --> 00:56:21,643
I don't know.

331
00:56:25,766 --> 00:56:29,267
What's that? A patrol?

332
00:56:30,312 --> 00:56:31,693
I don't see riders.

333
00:56:37,152 --> 00:56:37,993
Hold it!

334
00:56:41,323 --> 00:56:42,664
I saw them coming!

335
00:57:14,189 --> 00:57:17,320
At least this time...

336
00:57:18,026 --> 00:57:20,197
I was able to protect you.

337
00:58:31,266 --> 00:58:33,307
Caesar...

338
00:58:35,104 --> 00:58:37,401
This must stop...

339
00:58:37,481 --> 00:58:39,772
It's not too late to join the other apes...

340
00:58:40,609 --> 00:58:42,860
We cannot turn back!

341
00:58:44,113 --> 00:58:45,784
Luca gave his life!

342
00:58:46,323 --> 00:58:47,744
Please...

343
00:58:53,080 --> 00:58:54,461
They must pay.

344
00:59:00,963 --> 00:59:02,924
Now...

345
00:59:03,841 --> 00:59:06,642
...you sound like Koba.

346
00:59:13,100 --> 00:59:15,230
It was a mistake bringing you all.

347
00:59:15,310 --> 00:59:16,691
This is my fight.

348
00:59:18,105 --> 00:59:19,696
I will finish this alone.

349
00:59:21,358 --> 00:59:22,446
Go.

350
00:59:22,526 --> 00:59:23,647
Now!

351
00:59:24,445 --> 00:59:26,156
Join the others.

352
01:00:53,617 --> 01:00:56,698
What happened?

353
01:00:58,372 --> 01:01:02,043
They came out of nowhere...

354
01:01:02,543 --> 01:01:04,344
Attacked us.

355
01:01:05,587 --> 01:01:07,508
We thought they would kill us all...

356
01:01:07,923 --> 01:01:10,224
But the Colonel stopped them!

357
01:01:12,261 --> 01:01:13,974
There was madness in his eyes!

358
01:01:14,054 --> 01:01:18,935
He said they would use us, before we died!

359
01:01:19,601 --> 01:01:21,902
And they brought us all here!

360
01:01:23,605 --> 01:01:24,896
Use you?

361
01:01:26,942 --> 01:01:29,903
They've been forcing us to work!

362
01:01:31,113 --> 01:01:32,114
What...

363
01:01:32,948 --> 01:01:34,779
What kind of work?

364
01:01:37,536 --> 01:01:38,791
Wait.

365
01:01:38,871 --> 01:01:41,372
My little son. Is he here?

366
01:01:52,009 --> 01:01:55,100
Grant and Lee...

367
01:01:59,141 --> 01:02:01,022
Wellington...

368
01:02:02,811 --> 01:02:04,482
and Napoleon...

369
01:02:07,149 --> 01:02:08,360
Custer...

370
01:02:10,652 --> 01:02:12,493
and Sitting Bull...

371
01:02:15,282 --> 01:02:17,623
You're probably not much of a reader.

372
01:02:19,119 --> 01:02:22,290
But this is a big moment.

373
01:02:23,457 --> 01:02:25,128
Where were you?

374
01:02:26,293 --> 01:02:29,634
We came upon your herd. We got lucky.

375
01:02:30,631 --> 01:02:32,802
But I was surprised you weren't with them.

376
01:02:34,676 --> 01:02:36,007
Hey, hey, hey!

377
01:02:44,895 --> 01:02:48,186
I hope you don't come
to regret sparing his life.

378
01:02:49,733 --> 01:02:52,244
He's quite a good shot.

379
01:02:57,699 --> 01:03:00,870
Have you finally come to save your apes?

380
01:03:01,662 --> 01:03:03,917
I came for you.

381
01:03:03,997 --> 01:03:05,498
For me?

382
01:03:08,502 --> 01:03:10,799
Who did I kill that night?

383
01:03:10,879 --> 01:03:12,340
My wife.

384
01:03:14,049 --> 01:03:16,260
My son.

385
01:03:28,063 --> 01:03:29,734
I'm sorry.

386
01:03:30,399 --> 01:03:32,030
I was there for you.

387
01:03:43,036 --> 01:03:44,407
My God.

388
01:03:45,581 --> 01:03:47,712
Look at your eyes.

389
01:03:48,375 --> 01:03:49,996
Almost human.

390
01:03:54,381 --> 01:03:56,092
How did you know I was here?

391
01:03:56,633 --> 01:03:59,804
I was told you were coming.

392
01:04:00,888 --> 01:04:03,852
That more soldiers from the North...

393
01:04:03,932 --> 01:04:05,980
would be joining you here.

394
01:04:06,060 --> 01:04:07,231
Joining me?

395
01:04:07,311 --> 01:04:09,152
To finish us off.

396
01:04:10,564 --> 01:04:11,615
For good.

397
01:04:14,735 --> 01:04:16,246
Who told you that?

398
01:04:25,788 --> 01:04:26,789
Okay.

399
01:04:29,416 --> 01:04:30,417
Let's go.

400
01:05:09,456 --> 01:05:10,917
Father!

401
01:05:13,460 --> 01:05:14,671
Father!

402
01:06:37,002 --> 01:06:38,383
Lake...

403
01:06:39,213 --> 01:06:41,054
Forgive them.

404
01:06:41,382 --> 01:06:43,763
We've been through much.

405
01:06:51,100 --> 01:06:52,931
Father!

406
01:06:55,187 --> 01:06:56,938
What have I done?

407
01:07:35,394 --> 01:07:37,355
Battalion, halt!

408
01:07:42,651 --> 01:07:43,781
Blood!

409
01:07:43,861 --> 01:07:45,152
Makes the grass grow!

410
01:07:45,821 --> 01:07:46,825
We!

411
01:07:46,905 --> 01:07:48,236
Make the blood flow!

412
01:07:48,657 --> 01:07:49,912
We are the beginning!

413
01:07:49,992 --> 01:07:51,333
And the end!

414
01:09:34,930 --> 01:09:37,311
We haven't had food or water
since we got here...

415
01:09:43,439 --> 01:09:45,110
Why do they need a wall?

416
01:10:00,998 --> 01:10:02,079
Hey!

417
01:10:04,084 --> 01:10:05,635
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

418
01:10:19,516 --> 01:10:20,517
Hey!

419
01:10:21,477 --> 01:10:22,638
Donkey!

420
01:10:23,729 --> 01:10:24,900
Get him.

421
01:10:24,980 --> 01:10:26,691
Okay, okay, okay...

422
01:10:56,678 --> 01:10:57,849
Leave him!

423
01:13:37,297 --> 01:13:39,218
Tell them to get back to work.

424
01:13:39,633 --> 01:13:42,894
Apes need food and water.

425
01:13:45,848 --> 01:13:47,269
Tell them.

426
01:13:47,349 --> 01:13:49,438
Give them food...

427
01:13:49,518 --> 01:13:50,849
and water.

428
01:13:59,027 --> 01:14:00,108
Five...

429
01:14:01,405 --> 01:14:02,536
Four...

430
01:14:04,032 --> 01:14:05,123
Three...

431
01:14:07,077 --> 01:14:08,198
Two...

432
01:14:26,180 --> 01:14:29,221
Hurry! Back to work!

433
01:14:46,909 --> 01:14:48,410
String him up, donkey.

434
01:14:58,462 --> 01:15:01,053
Bad place.

435
01:15:03,133 --> 01:15:04,804
Bad, bad place.

436
01:15:07,846 --> 01:15:09,427
What you see?

437
01:15:15,604 --> 01:15:16,775
Must save them!

438
01:15:16,855 --> 01:15:17,985
But how?

439
01:15:18,065 --> 01:15:19,236
Must think!

440
01:15:19,483 --> 01:15:21,824
What would Caesar do?

441
01:15:23,112 --> 01:15:24,283
Oh, no!

442
01:15:26,949 --> 01:15:28,160
Why so small?

443
01:16:01,525 --> 01:16:03,696
What did the Colonel promise you?

444
01:16:04,361 --> 01:16:08,160
You really think he'll let you live...

445
01:16:08,240 --> 01:16:10,031
after we are gone?

446
01:16:11,160 --> 01:16:13,661
You let them call you "donkey."

447
01:16:14,121 --> 01:16:16,372
You are ape.

448
01:16:26,008 --> 01:16:28,639
Kerna want see you.

449
01:16:53,368 --> 01:16:58,085
Interfere with the work again and I'll
begin slaughtering the apes one by one.

450
01:16:58,165 --> 01:17:00,254
Understand? I need that wall.

451
01:17:00,334 --> 01:17:03,048
Apes need food and water.

452
01:17:03,128 --> 01:17:06,669
They'll get food and water
when they finish their work.

453
01:17:09,176 --> 01:17:11,797
Give apes food and water...

454
01:17:12,346 --> 01:17:14,018
or they cannot finish.

455
01:17:14,098 --> 01:17:16,429
You know, you are very emotional.

456
01:17:18,727 --> 01:17:21,898
What makes you think
you're in a position to make demands?

457
01:17:27,861 --> 01:17:29,116
Okay, let's go.

458
01:17:29,196 --> 01:17:30,993
The soldiers who are coming here...

459
01:17:31,073 --> 01:17:34,084
they are not coming to join you, are they?

460
01:17:35,744 --> 01:17:40,045
I saw men outside on the wall,
preparing for battle.

461
01:17:43,043 --> 01:17:44,673
They told me you were smart...

462
01:17:44,753 --> 01:17:47,801
but that's impressive.

463
01:17:47,881 --> 01:17:49,012
No.

464
01:17:49,883 --> 01:17:51,724
They won't be joining me.

465
01:17:52,094 --> 01:17:53,807
They are against you?

466
01:17:53,887 --> 01:17:56,393
They fear me.

467
01:17:56,473 --> 01:17:57,561
Why?

468
01:17:57,641 --> 01:18:00,272
Because you kill your own men?

469
01:18:01,270 --> 01:18:03,271
We found bodies.

470
01:18:03,939 --> 01:18:05,480
Something wrong...

471
01:18:05,983 --> 01:18:07,784
with these men.

472
01:18:10,487 --> 01:18:13,948
Jesus Christ, you are impressive.

473
01:18:14,450 --> 01:18:16,830
Well, you paint quite a picture.

474
01:18:16,910 --> 01:18:19,166
What you must think of me.

475
01:18:19,246 --> 01:18:22,617
I think you have no mercy.

476
01:18:40,851 --> 01:18:42,692
You came here to kill me.

477
01:18:43,979 --> 01:18:46,235
Were you gonna show me mercy?

478
01:18:46,315 --> 01:18:48,529
I showed you mercy...

479
01:18:48,609 --> 01:18:50,440
when I spared your men.

480
01:18:50,944 --> 01:18:53,409
I offered you peace...

481
01:18:53,489 --> 01:18:55,160
and you killed my family.

482
01:19:10,172 --> 01:19:11,303
Mercy.

483
01:19:12,466 --> 01:19:15,837
You have any idea
what your mercy would do to us?

484
01:19:20,057 --> 01:19:22,478
You're much stronger than we are.

485
01:19:23,018 --> 01:19:25,107
You're smart as hell.

486
01:19:25,187 --> 01:19:28,152
No matter what you say,
you'd eventually replace us.

487
01:19:28,232 --> 01:19:30,233
That's the law of nature.

488
01:19:31,026 --> 01:19:33,324
The irony is, we created you.

489
01:19:33,404 --> 01:19:36,327
We tried to defy nature, bend it to our will.

490
01:19:36,407 --> 01:19:39,788
Nature has been punishing us
for our arrogance...

491
01:19:39,868 --> 01:19:41,329
ever since.

492
01:19:43,789 --> 01:19:47,254
10 months ago, I sent out
recon units to look for your base.

493
01:19:47,334 --> 01:19:50,549
My own son was a soldier
with one of the units.

494
01:19:50,629 --> 01:19:52,420
One day he suddenly stopped speaking.

495
01:19:53,173 --> 01:19:56,013
He became primitive, like an animal.

496
01:19:56,093 --> 01:19:59,644
They contacted me and said
that they thought he'd lost his mind.

497
01:20:00,514 --> 01:20:02,685
That the war was too much for him.

498
01:20:03,684 --> 01:20:06,985
Then the man who cared for him
stopped speaking too.

499
01:20:08,063 --> 01:20:11,734
Their medic had a theory,
before he stopped speaking...

500
01:20:12,818 --> 01:20:15,908
that the virus that almost wiped us out...

501
01:20:15,988 --> 01:20:19,369
the virus that every human
survivor still carries...

502
01:20:19,700 --> 01:20:21,955
had suddenly changed.

503
01:20:22,035 --> 01:20:23,246
Mutated.

504
01:20:24,997 --> 01:20:27,252
And that if it spread...

505
01:20:27,332 --> 01:20:30,383
it would destroy humanity for good this time.

506
01:20:31,712 --> 01:20:33,133
Not by killing us...

507
01:20:33,213 --> 01:20:37,763
but by robbing us of those things
that make us human.

508
01:20:37,843 --> 01:20:39,894
Our speech, our higher thinking...

509
01:20:40,554 --> 01:20:42,685
It would turn us into beasts.

510
01:20:42,765 --> 01:20:44,776
You talk about mercy?

511
01:20:46,935 --> 01:20:48,896
What would you have done?

512
01:20:51,857 --> 01:20:54,278
It was a moment of clarity for me.

513
01:20:54,943 --> 01:20:56,198
I realized...

514
01:20:56,278 --> 01:20:59,451
that I would have to sacrifice my only son...

515
01:20:59,531 --> 01:21:02,532
so that humanity could be saved.

516
01:21:05,079 --> 01:21:07,167
I held that gun in my hand...

517
01:21:07,247 --> 01:21:09,748
for a long time.

518
01:21:14,088 --> 01:21:18,049
I pointed it at my only child...

519
01:21:20,594 --> 01:21:22,515
he looked at me...

520
01:21:23,889 --> 01:21:25,720
trust in his eyes.

521
01:21:28,727 --> 01:21:31,648
Even in his primitive gaze...

522
01:21:35,943 --> 01:21:39,284
I felt his... love.

523
01:21:46,412 --> 01:21:48,413
I pulled the trigger.

524
01:21:50,707 --> 01:21:51,958
It purified me.

525
01:21:53,961 --> 01:21:56,382
It made my purpose clear.

526
01:21:58,132 --> 01:22:02,306
I gave the orders to kill
the other infected. All of them.

527
01:22:02,386 --> 01:22:07,269
Burn their belongings and anything
that might spread contamination.

528
01:22:07,349 --> 01:22:10,022
Some of the men questioned my judgment.

529
01:22:10,102 --> 01:22:12,775
I was asking them to do what I had done.

530
01:22:12,855 --> 01:22:15,196
Sacrifice their friends...

531
01:22:16,358 --> 01:22:17,609
their family.

532
01:22:20,696 --> 01:22:22,447
Of course, they refused.

533
01:22:25,534 --> 01:22:27,205
So I had them killed too.

534
01:22:29,663 --> 01:22:32,127
Others with children...

535
01:22:32,207 --> 01:22:34,328
deserted into the woods.

536
01:22:35,335 --> 01:22:39,510
One of those cowards fled
to my superiors up North.

537
01:22:39,590 --> 01:22:43,971
They tried to convince me this plague
could be dealt with medically.

538
01:22:44,595 --> 01:22:48,436
That's when I realized
that they had learned nothing...

539
01:22:49,141 --> 01:22:50,732
from our past.

540
01:22:51,852 --> 01:22:54,523
You killed them too?

541
01:22:56,815 --> 01:22:58,726
What did I do, Preacher?

542
01:22:59,902 --> 01:23:01,573
You severed their heads, sir.

543
01:23:02,988 --> 01:23:05,285
Except for the one I spared...

544
01:23:05,365 --> 01:23:08,122
so that he could return,
and deliver a message.

545
01:23:08,202 --> 01:23:10,708
If they wanted to relieve me of my command...

546
01:23:10,788 --> 01:23:13,711
they would have to meet me here...

547
01:23:13,791 --> 01:23:15,838
and do it themselves.

548
01:23:15,918 --> 01:23:17,709
This used to be a weapons depot.

549
01:23:18,462 --> 01:23:23,223
They turned it into a relocation camp
when the crisis was just beginning.

550
01:23:23,717 --> 01:23:25,888
But the weapons are still here...

551
01:23:26,553 --> 01:23:28,142
inside the mountain.

552
01:23:28,222 --> 01:23:29,810
How many men...

553
01:23:29,890 --> 01:23:31,603
will be coming?

554
01:23:31,683 --> 01:23:34,940
Probably all of them.
But don't get any ideas.

555
01:23:35,020 --> 01:23:38,441
The only thing they fear more
than me is you apes.

556
01:23:45,322 --> 01:23:49,283
This is... a holy war.

557
01:23:50,828 --> 01:23:54,539
All of human history has led to this moment.

558
01:23:55,457 --> 01:23:57,248
If we lose...

559
01:23:58,043 --> 01:24:00,507
we'll be the last of our kind.

560
01:24:00,587 --> 01:24:03,128
It will be a planet of apes.

561
01:24:04,758 --> 01:24:06,759
And we will become your cattle.

562
01:24:08,887 --> 01:24:10,848
Look at you.

563
01:24:11,265 --> 01:24:13,686
You think I'm sick, don't you?

564
01:24:22,109 --> 01:24:24,860
I didn't mean to kill your son.

565
01:24:26,739 --> 01:24:30,620
But if his destiny was
to inherit your unholy kingdom...

566
01:24:32,453 --> 01:24:33,584
I'm glad I did it.

567
01:24:34,496 --> 01:24:36,117
Hey! Hey!

568
01:24:36,623 --> 01:24:38,214
Get back! Donkey, hold him!

569
01:24:38,751 --> 01:24:39,792
Hey!

570
01:24:47,176 --> 01:24:48,887
So emotional!

571
01:24:56,268 --> 01:24:58,849
I can see how conflicted you are.

572
01:24:59,730 --> 01:25:03,153
You're confused in your purpose.

573
01:25:03,233 --> 01:25:08,200
You are angry at me for something
I did that was an act of war.

574
01:25:08,280 --> 01:25:13,031
But you're taking this all
much too personally.

575
01:25:14,995 --> 01:25:16,956
What do you think...

576
01:25:17,247 --> 01:25:21,708
my men would have done
to your apes if you had killed me?

577
01:25:23,045 --> 01:25:25,516
Or is killing me more important?

578
01:25:38,227 --> 01:25:39,938
Soldiers everywhere!

579
01:25:40,187 --> 01:25:41,558
How will we get in?

580
01:25:43,065 --> 01:25:45,036
Must get in somehow...

581
01:25:45,442 --> 01:25:46,943
Must get in!

582
01:25:48,779 --> 01:25:50,030
In? In?

583
01:25:51,073 --> 01:25:52,074
No!

584
01:25:52,616 --> 01:25:54,907
No go in! No...

585
01:26:03,252 --> 01:26:04,965
Friends, friends!

586
01:26:05,045 --> 01:26:06,634
No, no go in.

587
01:26:06,714 --> 01:26:08,055
No go in...

588
01:26:11,844 --> 01:26:14,355
Friend! Friend!

589
01:26:18,100 --> 01:26:20,561
Thank you. Thank you, friend.

590
01:27:06,982 --> 01:27:09,363
You saved our lives!

591
01:27:50,484 --> 01:27:52,615
Sick humans...

592
01:27:52,903 --> 01:27:55,534
...must have escaped down here!

593
01:28:00,369 --> 01:28:02,207
No! No! No!

594
01:28:02,287 --> 01:28:04,828
No! No climb!

595
01:28:18,721 --> 01:28:19,512
What?

596
01:28:20,097 --> 01:28:21,718
What you see?

597
01:28:28,856 --> 01:28:30,567
Wonder where we are?

598
01:28:54,590 --> 01:28:57,381
Oh, no, friend!

599
01:29:01,138 --> 01:29:01,969
No!

600
01:29:03,599 --> 01:29:04,600
No!

601
01:29:05,768 --> 01:29:07,564
No! No!

602
01:29:07,644 --> 01:29:09,275
No! Come! Come!

603
01:29:13,859 --> 01:29:16,030
Come! Come back! Come!

604
01:29:17,112 --> 01:29:18,283
No, come!

605
01:29:18,989 --> 01:29:21,950
Come! Come! Come!

606
01:29:53,232 --> 01:29:54,653
Koba!

607
01:29:59,905 --> 01:30:01,316
Sleep.

608
01:30:02,324 --> 01:30:05,045
You cannot save them.

609
01:30:06,829 --> 01:30:10,290
Apes all die here.

610
01:30:13,293 --> 01:30:14,715
No!

611
01:30:14,795 --> 01:30:15,966
Yes.

612
01:30:17,965 --> 01:30:20,306
Join me.

613
01:30:36,608 --> 01:30:39,029
If he's still alive in the morning...

614
01:30:44,616 --> 01:30:47,537
he goes to work like everyone else...

615
01:30:48,454 --> 01:30:50,501
or you shoot him.

616
01:30:50,581 --> 01:30:53,712
Come! Come, come.

617
01:30:57,004 --> 01:30:58,845
She go in!

618
01:32:06,573 --> 01:32:08,534
Thirsty...

619
01:34:25,212 --> 01:34:26,253
Hide!

620
01:34:26,922 --> 01:34:27,923
Quick!

621
01:34:38,267 --> 01:34:40,348
Humans will kill her!

622
01:34:41,812 --> 01:34:44,113
I know what to do! Go!

623
01:34:53,031 --> 01:34:55,371
Arms up! Hey! Hey!

624
01:34:55,451 --> 01:34:56,992
Arms up!
Watch it! Watch it!

625
01:35:00,622 --> 01:35:01,623
Let's go!

626
01:35:03,751 --> 01:35:04,962
Keep 'em up!

627
01:35:09,089 --> 01:35:10,510
Follow him down.

628
01:35:14,762 --> 01:35:15,603
Keep them up!

629
01:36:17,408 --> 01:36:19,199
Are there others out there?

630
01:36:27,000 --> 01:36:28,341
Sweep the area.

631
01:36:29,503 --> 01:36:30,674
Put him in the pen.

632
01:37:14,256 --> 01:37:17,797
Feeling better?

633
01:37:23,015 --> 01:37:23,856
Good.

634
01:37:24,141 --> 01:37:25,852
Then we can talk about...

635
01:37:26,643 --> 01:37:28,194
Escape.

636
01:37:29,104 --> 01:37:31,065
Apes together strong!

637
01:37:40,282 --> 01:37:41,578
We are the beginning!

638
01:37:41,658 --> 01:37:42,869
And the end!

639
01:38:06,683 --> 01:38:08,394
Still alive.

640
01:38:39,925 --> 01:38:41,336
Send him to the quarry. Alone.

641
01:38:45,264 --> 01:38:46,435
Hold on.

642
01:39:05,576 --> 01:39:06,947
What is this?

643
01:39:11,123 --> 01:39:12,754
How did this get in there?

644
01:39:16,044 --> 01:39:17,255
Get him to work.

645
01:39:31,060 --> 01:39:32,691
Thirty-seven.

646
01:39:43,447 --> 01:39:44,568
Fifty-five.

647
01:39:47,034 --> 01:39:49,245
Thirty-seven steps to the adult cage...

648
01:39:49,661 --> 01:39:51,752
Fifty-five to the children.

649
01:40:30,744 --> 01:40:32,541
You know...

650
01:40:32,621 --> 01:40:34,372
Kerna shoot apes...

651
01:40:34,915 --> 01:40:36,416
when wall is done.

652
01:40:40,170 --> 01:40:43,171
His wall is madness.

653
01:40:44,299 --> 01:40:45,720
It won't save him...

654
01:40:47,678 --> 01:40:49,892
any more than it will save you.

655
01:40:49,972 --> 01:40:51,773
I save myself.

656
01:40:53,016 --> 01:40:58,437
Is there anything left of you to save?

657
01:41:20,419 --> 01:41:21,630
I do.

658
01:41:39,229 --> 01:41:40,810
Apes going back to the cage?

659
01:41:44,735 --> 01:41:46,156
You...

660
01:41:46,862 --> 01:41:47,993
Are very brave.

661
01:41:49,490 --> 01:41:50,661
Brave?

662
01:41:50,908 --> 01:41:52,029
Brave!

663
01:41:52,743 --> 01:41:54,204
Brave!

664
01:41:59,166 --> 01:42:00,327
Ape?

665
01:42:02,669 --> 01:42:03,670
Me...

666
01:42:03,962 --> 01:42:05,513
Ape?

667
01:42:13,347 --> 01:42:14,678
You are...

668
01:42:27,194 --> 01:42:29,035
Nova.

669
01:42:31,281 --> 01:42:32,492
Nova.

670
01:42:43,794 --> 01:42:45,841
Come! Come! Come see!

671
01:42:45,921 --> 01:42:47,132
Come see!

672
01:42:47,923 --> 01:42:50,434
Come! Come see!

673
01:43:05,441 --> 01:43:08,152
34, 35, 36, 37...

674
01:43:09,319 --> 01:43:10,320
37!

675
01:43:12,740 --> 01:43:14,071
I do.

676
01:43:16,660 --> 01:43:17,831
What now?

677
01:43:26,420 --> 01:43:27,251
What?

678
01:43:33,844 --> 01:43:35,855
Oh, no!

679
01:43:36,513 --> 01:43:37,644
Oh, no!

680
01:43:38,640 --> 01:43:40,062
No, no!

681
01:43:40,142 --> 01:43:41,353
No, no, no...

682
01:43:46,815 --> 01:43:48,066
Okay.

683
01:44:54,007 --> 01:44:56,588
This is the ape I told you about!

684
01:44:58,679 --> 01:45:00,390
Thank you.

685
01:45:17,656 --> 01:45:19,027
Bad Ape.

686
01:45:39,678 --> 01:45:40,639
What's wrong?

687
01:46:00,616 --> 01:46:01,737
We can't keep digging!

688
01:46:02,076 --> 01:46:04,237
It will flood the whole tunnel!

689
01:46:04,495 --> 01:46:07,296
If we don't, we can't reach the children!

690
01:46:26,975 --> 01:46:28,636
We must keep looking down there...

691
01:46:28,977 --> 01:46:30,808
Find another way to reach the children....

692
01:46:31,188 --> 01:46:32,939
We must leave now!

693
01:46:33,232 --> 01:46:34,653
More soldiers are coming!

694
01:46:35,109 --> 01:46:36,650
Humans will destroy each other!

695
01:46:37,069 --> 01:46:38,950
And us with them!

696
01:46:43,617 --> 01:46:45,448
We'll have to get the children out
above ground!

697
01:46:46,328 --> 01:46:47,449
How...

698
01:47:21,697 --> 01:47:22,698
Hey!

699
01:47:24,199 --> 01:47:25,530
You animals!

700
01:47:45,929 --> 01:47:47,010
Who did that?

701
01:47:48,182 --> 01:47:49,523
Who did that?

702
01:47:51,351 --> 01:47:52,392
Huh?

703
01:47:54,146 --> 01:47:55,517
Who was it?

704
01:48:03,530 --> 01:48:04,741
Was it you?

705
01:49:57,519 --> 01:49:58,980
I love you, son.

706
01:51:08,799 --> 01:51:10,680
Go, go, go.

707
01:51:28,444 --> 01:51:29,785
Hurry! Let's go!

708
01:51:34,783 --> 01:51:36,624
Caesar, what's wrong?

709
01:51:47,296 --> 01:51:48,917
Hurry, you must go.

710
01:51:49,923 --> 01:51:51,764
Without you?

711
01:51:52,384 --> 01:51:54,181
No...

712
01:51:54,261 --> 01:51:55,972
Maurice was right.

713
01:52:00,851 --> 01:52:02,482
I am...

714
01:52:03,520 --> 01:52:04,811
like Koba.

715
01:52:05,856 --> 01:52:06,977
He could not...

716
01:52:08,150 --> 01:52:10,031
escape his hate.

717
01:52:16,116 --> 01:52:18,447
And I still cannot escape mine.

718
01:52:24,833 --> 01:52:26,384
Go, go, go.

719
01:52:28,796 --> 01:52:29,797
Fire!

720
01:53:13,173 --> 01:53:15,514
Colonel! Colonel!

721
01:53:17,928 --> 01:53:19,349
Where the hell is he?

722
01:53:53,088 --> 01:53:55,509
Down! Down! Down!

723
01:53:56,967 --> 01:53:58,178
Get down!

724
01:58:12,973 --> 01:58:14,524
Take him out!

725
01:58:26,195 --> 01:58:28,326
Come on, donkey. Let's go! Reload!

726
01:59:03,857 --> 01:59:06,358
Colonel, are you in there? Colonel!

727
01:59:07,027 --> 01:59:08,568
Just break it down.

728
01:59:48,694 --> 01:59:49,575
Donkey!

729
01:59:50,404 --> 01:59:51,785
Grenade launcher!

730
02:00:48,962 --> 02:00:52,013
God damn it, donkey! Get me the launcher!

731
02:05:01,048 --> 02:05:04,179
Oh, no! Oh, no!

732
02:05:04,259 --> 02:05:06,220
Oh, no! Oh, no!

733
02:09:11,799 --> 02:09:13,470
Don't worry.

734
02:09:18,055 --> 02:09:19,476
Maurice.

735
02:09:23,310 --> 02:09:27,811
You are all home now.

736
02:09:31,693 --> 02:09:33,864
Apes are strong.

737
02:09:37,950 --> 02:09:39,201
With...

738
02:09:40,411 --> 02:09:42,292
or without me.

739
02:10:09,398 --> 02:10:11,149
Son...

740
02:10:13,610 --> 02:10:15,611
will know...

741
02:10:17,072 --> 02:10:18,493
who...

742
02:10:19,742 --> 02:10:21,123
was...

743
02:10:22,411 --> 02:10:23,752
father.

744
02:10:34,715 --> 02:10:36,306
And what...

745
02:10:38,469 --> 02:10:39,970
Caesar...

746
02:10:43,098 --> 02:10:44,389
did...

747
02:10:45,893 --> 02:10:47,394
for us.

748
02:11:53,127 --> 02:11:54,788
Caesar...

